abstract: >
  GraphSplit is a standard-library-only Julia implementation of sparse,
  graph-based earthquake relocation from synchronized DDSync theta data. It
  includes native Cartesian and radial layered-model travel-time builders,
  robust matrix-free inversion, serial-ID-safe catalog/common initialization,
  HypoDD-style corrected origin times, cumulative space-time shift sidecars,
  physical and fixed-depth constraints, conditional station-phase bootstrap
  and linearized uncertainty, and TOML-driven reproducible runs.
